  "control": "ttnn.multiply takes a dtype and no compute_kernel_config, so the lever and its control are the same knob in opposite directions. Forcing the product to bf16 on the fp32 arm degrades 1.5653x / 2.6643x / 2.3640x / 2.1735x at K = 20.4 / 2.1e+04 / 2.1e+05 / 2.1e+06, so the knob reaches the kernel and the null is a null.",
  "question": "autograd.py:1611 forms _sum_leadings summands with ttnn.multiply(g, norm), which passes no dtype. Does forcing the product to fp32 move the HIGH-K rungs?",
  "verdict": "REFUTED on the fp32 arm and worth ~1.1x on the bf16 arm. On fp32 activations the summands are ALREADY fp32 -- recorded from inside the rule, g=FLOAT32 norm=FLOAT32 prod=FLOAT32 -- and forcing fp32 is BIT-IDENTICAL at every rung including K=2.1e+06. On bf16 activations the summands are bf16 and forcing fp32 moves the headline 0.87x to 1.03x. Neither is the ~800-7000x device-vs-host-fp32 floor."
 },
