  "cosine_correction": "amendment 5 reads the ladders cosine as never going negative. One arm does: fp32 activations, fp32 weights, K=2.1e+06 reads cos -0.019878. A random direction in 384 dimensions has |cos| ~ 0.051, so -0.02 is what a fully error-dominated result looks like and the mechanism can reach cos <= 0. It cannot reach the -0.796 and -0.805 that blocks 0 and 6 read, which are ~16 sigma from zero. The conclusion stands in its strong form and the evidence for it is the DISTANCE from zero, not the sign.",
  "question": "the leafs own 24 blocks split 15 on-curve / 9 off-curve. Is block 8 simply higher-K than block 9?",
