  "question": "amendment 6 hands over the 23.8917 % of the arm no softmax lever touches, whose largest member is conditioned_transition.layer_norm.layer_norm_s.weight at 15.5125 % of the model and mass-weighted rel 0.1828.",
  "verdict": "the conditioned transition is NOT broken. Run alone on the real (a, s) the block hands it, against upstream 0.4.3s own ConditionedTransitionBlock in float64, all 9 of its parameter gradients read 5.5e-03 to 9.7e-03 at blocks 8, 9 and 0, mass-weighted 5.468736e-03 / 7.278610e-03 / 9.595681e-03, 0 of 9 over the 5.0e-02 per-tensor bar and inside the 2.0e-02 mass bar, with cos >= 0.99997 and norm ratios within 1 % of unity. Feeding it OUR blocks `a` instead of the references moves it at most 1.44x and at block 0 slightly improves it. The models 0.1828 is not made inside this module.",
  "what_it_leaves": "the 0.1828 must be carried by the cotangent that arrives at the transitions output -- from the blocks above it, the atom decoder, or the accumulation over 48 samples. Extrapolating this arms slope (rel ~ 1.55e-04 x K at K 35.7) the transition would need K ~ 1.2e+03 to reach 0.1828, against the K 10.5 to 35.8 measured here."
 },
