 "instrument_correction": {
  "after": "mha.linear_o.weight 2.492647e-02 cos 0.999740, mha.linear_g.weight 2.469198e-02 cos 0.999853 -- both ordinary. No defect there.",
  "cause": "both are 768x768. The instrument inferred the transpose from the shape, which cannot disambiguate a square matrix, so the device gradient was compared against the references transpose.",
  "fix": "read the flag `_DiTBlock._w_tt` already records in its `(key, transpose)` cache key.",
  "lesson": "a transpose inferred from shape is silent on a square weight, and it manufactures exactly the r ~ 1 / cos ~ 0 signature this row taught everyone to read as a wrong transform.",
  "what": "the first widened block arm reported attention_pair_bias.mha.linear_o.weight and mha.linear_g.weight at rel 1.411 with r ~ 0.996 and cos ~ 0.0001 -- the textbook signature of a wrong transform."
 },
 "mechanism": "the disagreement is a device precision floor amplified by the conditioning of the LayerNorm-gain reduction. rel grows LINEARLY in K = sum_i||term_i|| / ||sum_i term_i||, the cancellation ratio of the gain gradient's own sum over tokens. A generic input gives K ~ 20 and rel ~ 2e-03; the published rel 18.504 sits between the K = 2.1e+05 and K = 2.1e+06 rungs of the ladder below.",
